{"term":"gulf","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:b2625de5a83b733e76","definition":"A hollow place in the earth; an abyss; a deep chasm or basin.","example":"He then surveyed / Hell and the gulf between.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["engulf","Gulf Coast","Gulf County","Gulf Creek","gulflike","Gulfport","Gulf Stream","Gulf War","gulfward","gulfwards","gulfweed","gulfy","Newgulf","Roper Gulf","The Gulf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gulf#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7650a20f3c04da037b","definition":"That which swallows; the gullet.","example":"Witch's mummy, maw and gulf / Of the ravined salt sea shark,","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["engulf","Gulf Coast","Gulf County","Gulf Creek","gulflike","Gulfport","Gulf Stream","Gulf War","gulfward","gulfwards","gulfweed","gulfy","Newgulf","Roper Gulf","The Gulf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gulf#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7b21c15e174765e87b","definition":"That which swallows irretrievably; a whirlpool; a sucking eddy.","example":"[T]here is no such mine, / None; but a gulf of ruin, swallowing gold, not making.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["engulf","Gulf Coast","Gulf County","Gulf Creek","gulflike","Gulfport","Gulf Stream","Gulf War","gulfward","gulfwards","gulfweed","gulfy","Newgulf","Roper Gulf","The Gulf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gulf#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:24ce705916d68d81fe","definition":"A portion of an ocean or sea extendi