y around and singling out Sullivan as a prime example.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["abyss","rift"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively","wordFamily":["engulf","Gulf Coast","Gulf County","Gulf Creek","gulflike","Gulfport","Gulf Stream","Gulf War","gulfward","gulfwards","gulfweed","gulfy","Newgulf","Roper Gulf","The Gulf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gulf#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c57c9582879ba16d74","definition":"The bottom part of a list of those awarded a degree, for those who have only just passed.","example":"Some ten or fifteen men just on the line, not enough to be plucked or good enough to be placed, are put into the \"gulf,\" as it is popularly called (the Examiners' phrase is \"Degrees allowed\"), and have their degrees given to them but are not printed in the calendar, nor were they at this time allowed to try for the Classical Tripos.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["engulf","Gulf Coast","Gulf County","Gulf Creek","gulflike","Gulfport","Gulf Stream","Gulf War","gulfward","gulfwards","gulfweed","gulfy","Newgulf","Roper Gulf","The Gulf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gulf#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e51a85908236873e5c","definition":"To engulf.","example":"[…] if with thee the roaring wells\n⁠Should gulf him fathom-deep in brine;\n⁠And hands so often clasp’d in mine,\nShould toss with tangle and with shells.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["engulf","Gulf Coast","Gulf County","Gulf Creek","gulflike","Gulfport","Gulf Stream","Gulf War","gulfward","gulfwards","gulfweed","gulfy","Newgulf","Roper Gulf","The Gulf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gulf#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:29df1a3162a56602c9","definition":"To award a degree to somebody who has only just passed sufficiently.","example":"The mention of gulfed and plucked men brings me back to myself.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["engulf","Gulf Coast","Gulf County","Gulf Creek","gulflike","Gulfport","Gulf Stream","Gulf War","gulfward","gulfwards","gulfweed","gulfy","Newgulf","Roper Gulf","The Gulf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gulf#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a403093134d37c5200","definition":"The Persian Gulf, or the region surrounding it.","example":"Gulf States","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["engulf","Gulf Coast","Gulf County","Gulf Creek","gulflike","Gulfport","Gulf Stream","Gulf War","gulfward","gulfwards","gulfweed","gulfy","Newgulf","Roper Gulf","The Gulf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Gulf#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0aefde6bcfef1f68f9","definition":"The Gulf of Mexico, or the region surrounding it.","example":"Gulf States","pos":"name","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["engulf","Gulf Coast","Gulf County","Gulf Creek","gulflike","Gulfport","Gulf Stream","Gulf War","gulfward","gulfwards","gulfweed","gulfy","Newgulf","Roper Gulf","The Gulf"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Gulf#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2193fec88e0cabb346","definiti